/T (The prototype measures one CPU-bound workload on one machine. Its results may differ for memory-bound, I/O-bound, or very short tasks, and on machines with different core layouts or NUMA structure. The dynamic method uses a Python multiprocessing queue, whose overhead is included in the measured time. The current version does not directly count migrations or cache misses; any statement about those effects will be treated as a possible explanation unless perf measurements are added.)
