/Title (on which core and when. A good scheduling decision keeps every core busy and lets a thread keep using the data already stored in the cache of the core it ran on. A poor decision can leave some cores idle while others are overloaded, or can move a thread to a new core where its cached data is lost. [4])
/Dest [10 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 353 0 R
/Prev 409 0 R
/Next 517 0 R
>>
