/Title (From the papers I reviewed, I understood that cache affinity, load balancing, and thread placement are important for multi-core performance. Previous work studies kernel scheduler behaviour, affinity policies, dynamic work distribution, and NUMA placement mostly as separate topics.)
/Dest [11 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 411 0 R
/Next 461 0 R
>>
endobj
461 0 obj
<<
/Title (I want to investigate the combined effect of processor affinity and workload distribution in a simple, controlled Python + Linux experiment, supported by an optional Rust kernel. I will keep the workload, the number of tasks, and the machine the same, while changing only the affinity setting and the distribution method. I am not claiming that previous research has never investigated these factors.)
/Dest [11 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 411 0 R
/Prev 460 0 R
>>
endobj
