/Title (This research investigates how processor affinity and workload distribution affect execution performance on a multi-core Linux system. The prototype uses multiple worker processes, optional core pinning, and three methods of distributing tasks. Execution time, throughput, and load imbalance are measured for different configurations.)
/Dest [16 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 412 0 R
/Next 465 0 R
>>
endobj
465 0 obj
<<
/Title (The experiment is intended to identify which combination of affinity and distribution gives better performance for the selected workload. The final conclusion will be based on the measured values and graphs, and will explain whether the results support the hypotheses.)
/Dest [16 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 412 0 R
/Prev 464 0 R
>>
endobj
